WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.344
Now things are changing for your project, and for Andy's too.

00:00:03.344 --> 00:00:08.388
[SOUND] I've got Andy on speed dial, number four.

00:00:08.388 --> 00:00:11.320
Hey Andy can you come down to my desk for a second?

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:11.965
Great, thanks.

00:00:11.965 --> 00:00:12.776
[SOUND] Now,

00:00:12.776 --> 00:00:17.817
the project manager has changed the requirements in two different ways.

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:20.210
First of all, there's not one cat anymore.

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:21.920
Now there are two cats.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:25.900
Second of all, the cat name should be above the cat image.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:29.880
So how you implement that is completely up to you, but

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.200
I would recommend avoiding the most naive of solutions.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.880
Don't just hardcode the cat name and the dom, or in the document.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.560
Instead, store that in a JavaScript variable, and then update the document.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:43.190
Hey Andy.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:44.050
&gt;&gt; Hey, what's up?

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.019
&gt;&gt; So the project requirements have changed.

00:00:46.019 --> 00:00:46.720
&gt;&gt; Okay.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:48.520
Cat clicker duo.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:49.940
&gt;&gt; Ooh, let me guess.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:50.740
Two cats?

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:51.350
&gt;&gt; Two cats.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.290
Can you do it?

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:56.430
&gt;&gt; I didn't plan for that, but I think I could probably figure it out.

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:56.930
&gt;&gt; Awesome.

